<span id="A2.T4.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:55.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T4.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T4.2.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ChainofDraft</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T4.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T4.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:150.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T4.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within <math id="A2.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\backslash" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>\</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\backslash</annotation></semantics></math>boxed{}. Keep a minimum draft for each thinking step, with 5 words at most.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Prompts for compared baselines.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ B.2 Details of Baselines ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Merlin’s Whisper: Enabling Efficient Reasoning in LLMs via Black-box Adversarial Prompting1Caution: this paper includes adversarial text that may be considered offensive." class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> presents the detailed prompts used for the baseline methods in our main experiments. For the <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NoThinking</span> baseline, we adopt the official prompt formats provided for the Qwen3 and DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen models. To explicitly suppress intermediate reasoning steps, we append “<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;think&gt;<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\backslash" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>\</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\backslash</annotation></semantics></math>n<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\backslash" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>\</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\backslash</annotation></semantics></math>n&lt;/think&gt;<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\backslash" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>\</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\backslash</annotation></semantics></math>n<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\backslash" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>\</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\backslash</annotation></semantics></math>n</span>” after the <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">assistant</span> indicator. For DEER <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2025c)</a></cite>, we use the original code implementation <span id="footnote11" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">11</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">11</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">11</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/iie-ycx/DEER" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/iie-ycx/DEER</a></span></span></span> to reproduce all results faithfully. To ensure a fair comparison across methods, we configure the <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">think_ratio</span> hyperparameter to 1.0, which is equal to the maximum generation length.</p>
</div>
</section>
